  "client_cases_comment": "Raw answers both clients must treat alike. hello_cases: the fake server's answer to the hello; {BODY} is a valid hello body (fields in 'set' replaced by raw JSON text), {LEN} its length; expect is a reason or 'verified'. answer_cases: the answer to the one request after a good hello, then the server closes; expect is 'ok <status> <body length>', 'error <message>' or 'refused'. {PAD:n} is n letters x.",
